---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import regions from "../../public/regions.json";
import provs from "../../public/providers.json";

const PROV = Object.fromEntries(provs.providers.map(p => [p.id, p]));
const eras = regions.regions.reduce((a, r) => a + r.eras.length, 0);
/* A region's own centre, so a map link lands on the ground being described
   rather than wherever the reader happened to leave the map. */
const mid = (r) => [
  (Math.min(...r.ring.map(p => p[0])) + Math.max(...r.ring.map(p => p[0]))) / 2,
  (Math.min(...r.ring.map(p => p[1])) + Math.max(...r.ring.map(p => p[1]))) / 2,
].map(n => Math.round(n * 1000) / 1000);
---
<Base
  title="Whose archive"
  eyebrow={`${regions.regions.length} record regions · ${eras} eras`}
  dek="A record region is a piece of ground whose records were filed the same way, and an era is a stretch of years over which that stayed true. This is the table the map reads when you set a year — and the reason it can tell you that a Croatian village's 1930 baptism is filed under Italy.">

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:20px;border-left-color:var(--accent)">
    <div class="prose">
      <p><b>Knowing who ruled a place is trivia. Knowing whose archive that means is research.</b>
      Every history of Istria will tell you it was Italian between the wars. What almost none of
      them tell you is the consequence: that the parish registers of those years were filmed by
      FamilySearch into a collection called <em>Italy, Pola and Trieste</em>, so a search of the
      Croatian collection returns nothing at all — and nothing looks exactly like a record that
      does not exist.</p>
      <p>That is the column this table adds. <a href={u("/")}>Set a year on the map</a> and it
      appears in every panel.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:20px">{regions.precision}</p>

  {regions.regions.map(r => (
    <section style="margin-top:38px">
      <h2><a href={u(`/region/${r.id}/`)}>{r.label}</a></h2>
      <p class="cap" style="margin-top:2px">{r.sub}</p>
      <table style="margin-top:12px">
        <thead><tr>
          <th class="m">Years</th><th>Who held it</th><th>Whose archive that means</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {r.eras.map(e => (
            <tr>
              {/* Every era row is a way into the map with that span set. The
                  table is the answer; the map is what you do with it. */}
              <td class="m"><a
                href={u(`/?layers=shelf,jurisdiction&years=${e.from},${e.to}&view=${mid(r)[0]},${mid(r)[1]},8`)}
                title={`See ${r.label} between ${e.from} and ${e.to}`}>{e.from}–{e.to}</a></td>
              <td>
                <span class="reg" style={`--c:var(${regions.regimes[e.regime].var})`}>
                  <i></i>{e.polity || regions.regimes[e.regime].label}
                </span>
              </td>
              <td>
                {e.filedUnder.length ? (
                  <span>{e.filedUnder.map((f, i) => (
                    <>{i > 0 && " · "}<a href={u(`/archive/${f}/`)}>{PROV[f].name}</a></>
                  ))}</span>
                ) : <span class="none">no registers survive</span>}
                {e.note && <p class={"enote" + (e.note.startsWith("THE ") ? " trap" : "")}>{e.note}</p>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  ))}

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:38px;border-left-color:var(--rule-strong)">
    <div class="lab">Six regions is not the world</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>These are the regions whose filing this project has actually worked out, which is the
      ground the Croatian shelf sits on. <b>A place outside them says so in its own panel</b>
      rather than guessing, because a confident wrong answer about which archive to write to
      costs somebody a month.</p>
      <p><a href={u("/add/")}>Know a region's filing history? That is the most valuable thing
      you could contribute →</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 500; margin: 0; }
  td { vertical-align: top; }
  .reg { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 7px; }
  .reg i { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--c);
           display: inline-block; flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .none { color: var(--ink-3); font-style: italic; }
  .enote { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.55;
           color: var(--ink-3); margin: 6px 0 0; max-width: 60ch; }
  .enote.trap { color: var(--ink-2); border-left: 2px solid #C0392B;
                padding-left: 9px; }
</style>
